    "status": "implemented-after-baseline",
    "conclusion": "measured-win",
    "semantics": "The grain caller supplies a hint only when scalar particle_count remains strictly greater than 10 after conversion to the float32 value used by MLX, and scalar uniformity is in [0,1]. This proves lambda = particle_count / saturation > 10 for every pixel. Python 10.0000001, which rounds to float32 10.0, is explicitly rejected; nextafter(float32(10), +inf) is accepted. The MLX sampler then returns the original normal_clamped branch before constructing 60 unused Knuth rounds. RNG key, normal samples, rounding and clamp are unchanged. Unhinted mixed, NaN, negative, empty and infinity inputs retain the legacy graph with no added device reduction or host sync.",
